cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  For reproducible work, cite the exact BrainLearn version and commit used in
  the analysis. This metadata describes the in-development software; it is not
  a release or archival DOI.
type: software
title: >-
  BrainLearn: local-first visual workflows for reproducible neuroscience
  research
authors:
  - family-names: Sadeghi
    given-names: Mohammad
version: "0.1.0"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/Brain-Learn/brainlearn
url: https://brain-learn.github.io/brainlearn/
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - EEG
  - reproducible research
  - workflow builder
abstract: >-
  BrainLearn is a local-first visual workflow builder for reproducible
  neuroscience research. Its current EEG workflow is experimental and has not
  received independent scientific methods approval.
